  "reflectionText": "Mordecai went out of the king's presence in royal blue and white, with a great crown of gold, and the city of Susa shouted and was glad. The Jews had light, gladness, joy, and honor. Mourning gave way to feasting in courtyards from Shushan to the far ends of the empire. What is it to walk into a feast on a day that had been written down for your destruction?"
